      "content": "![Thousands of glowing rice-paper sky lanterns rising into the night sky of Chiang Mai](https://assets.lingocafe.app/traditions-04/images/loi-krathong-yi-peng-sky-lanterns-chiang-mai-hero.webp)\n\nCoinciding with the full moon of the twelfth lunar month in the traditional Thai calendar, the dual festivals of *Loi Krathong* and *Yi Peng* transform Chiang Mai—the historic capital of the ancient Lanna Kingdom—into one of the most visually poetic celebrations on Earth. While Loi Krathong is observed nationwide to express gratitude to the water spirit Phra Mae Khongkha for sustenance and seek forgiveness for river pollution, Yi Peng is a northern Lanna tradition of celestial merit-making rooted in Buddhist cosmology.\n\nThe material craft of the *krathong* showcases Thai botanical ingenuity. Using cylindrical slices of banana tree trunks as buoyant rafts, artisans fold glossy banana leaves into *kanok* patterns resembling lotus petals, topping them with scented jasmine garlands, marigolds, incense, and candles. Pilgrims place hair clippings or coin offerings inside to represent the expulsion of negative karma. Kneeling by the sluggish waters of the Mae Ping River, celebrants launch their vessels, watching currents transform the river into an undulating field of floating golden flames.\n\n![Floating banana-leaf krathong decorated with yellow marigolds, orchids, and a candle](https://assets.lingocafe.app/traditions-04/images/loi-krathong-yi-peng-sky-lanterns-chiang-mai-detail.webp)\n\nSimultaneously, the heavens are illuminated by the synchronized release of *khom loi*—cylindrical sky lanterns fashioned from oiled rice paper on gossamer bamboo frames. As the kerosene-soaked paraffin disc warms the enclosed air, the lanterns tug weightlessly against fingers before being released in unison. Within minutes, the starry canopy dissolves into an ascending galaxy of golden sparks. Witnessing this reciprocal luminescence—thousands of flames navigating the waters below while thousands drift through the heavens above—imparts an unforgettable sensation of universal peace, renewal, and spiritual release."
